        <content type="html" xml:base="https://ymiuraaa.github.io/blog/math-typesetting/">&lt;p&gt;Recall from elementary school the generalized Stokes&#x27; theorem: for an orientable manifold $M$ and differential form $\omega$,&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$$
\int_{\partial M} \omega = \int_M d\omega.
$$&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
